Let spills reach beyond the 128 KB that HWord scratch block messages can address.
Their 12-bit offset is relative to the scratch base in r0.5; without LSC (Gen12LP and
older) larger offsets used to wrap around, so spills overwrote private memory or other
spill slots. Keep the full offset in the spill/fill intrinsics and move r0.5 around
messages that start past the limit.

